# Header rules. netlify.toml [[headers]] is the primary source; this file must mirror it,
# because Netlify applies BOTH and a path can match rules in each.
#
# Deliberately no "X-Robots-Tag: index, follow" on /*: index,follow is already the default,
# so it added nothing, but /* also matches the .md twins and sent them a second directive
# contradicting their noindex. See the /*.md rule below.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Markdown twins for AI agents — keep out of the search index so they can't compete with
# the canonical HTML as duplicate content. Mirrors netlify.toml.
/*.md
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, follow
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# Cache static assets.
#
# CSS and JS mirror netlify.toml (one day + a week of stale-while-revalidate),
# per this file's own contract above. These two lines used to say one year,
# immutable — contradicting the toml — and that mattered for money: the
# immutable HTTP cache also satisfied the service worker's background
# revalidation, so after a price change a returning visitor could keep seeing
# and being charged the OLD prices until the cache expired. Price-critical
# scripts additionally carry a ?v= content hash stamped by pricing:apply, so
# a change is a new URL regardless of what any cache believes.
/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
